    /* :global on every DESCENDANT of .cd-table, and only there.
       WHY. The script builds the rows and the footer of the working table with
       document.createElement, so those cells never carry the astro- scope attribute. Astro appends
       that attribute to the last compound selector, so a plain `.cd-table tbody td` rule compiles
       to `td.astro-xxxx` and silently misses every generated cell: the working table rendered with
       no padding, no rules and no yellow product column, while the server rendered worked example
       two sections down looked correct. Anchoring on .cd-table, which IS in the static markup and
       so still carries the scope, keeps these rules on this page while letting them reach cells
       the script made. Same class of problem the rent vs buy calculator solves with :global(.mo).
       The .cd-table-letters and .cd-table-limits overrides below stay scoped, because both of
       those tables are entirely server rendered. */
